                  %a{:href => "#Mueller18"} Müller 18
          %p
            From
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#Crivellin18"} Crivellin 18, p. 2
          %blockquote
            %p
              the global fit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+anomalies"} flavour anomalies
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              even shows compelling evidence for New Physics
              = succeed "\u2026" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              The vector leptoquark (LQ)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)_L
              singlet with hypercharge
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -4/3
              arising in the famous
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pati-Salam+model"} Pati-Salam model
              is capable of explaining all the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+anomalies"} flavour
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              anomalies and therefore several attempts to construct a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/UV+completion"} UV completion
              for this LQ to address the anomalies have been made. It can give a sizeable effect in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo →
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi τ
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \to c(u)\tau \nu
              data without violating bounds from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo →
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ν
                    %mover
                      %mi ν
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \to s(d)\nu \bar \nu
              and/or direct searches, provides (at
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree+level"} tree level
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 9
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 10
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_9 = - C_{10}
              solution to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo →
                    %mi s
                    %msup
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mo −
